# Two suns: a warm key from high on one side, a cool fill from the opposite side.
# These were BOTH `light directional 0 0 0`, i.e. authored at the world origin. The
# direction is normalize(position - target) and the aim is hardcoded to the origin,
# so that made the direction normalize(vec3(0)) -> NaN in the shader: the light
# contributed nothing, still burned a slot in the 32-light budget, and counted as an
# "active light", which suppressed the camera fill light as well.
light directional -40 -30 60 255 228 190 1
light directional 50 40 30 165 175 200 1
